{"step_index":132,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-30T21:51:21Z","thinking":"The existing configuration appears to handle static file serving. Now, analyzing the design specifications to identify specific color palette requests and section styling guidelines. Recognizing the need to translate these color codes and section-specific design requests into actionable steps for visual redesign.\n\n\nConsidering design specifications, focusing on implementing the visual branding elements like readable text contrast and animations to achieve a premium feel. Expanding the food menu necessitates creation of food categories with required elements such as vegetarian indicators, best seller badges, filters, search bar, and add-to-cart functionality, driven by an editable data file. A functional shopping cart requires features for product addition/removal, quantity modifications, price calculation, and persistence using local storage, alongside a cart drawer animation. Finally, the checkout workflow requires input validation, a final order summary, and order ID generation with redirection to a tracking page.\n\n\nCustomer location features must allow geolocation, manual address entry, and map-based adjustment, displaying distance, time, and availability based on configurable restaurant coordinates and a distance radius using straight-line and road-route distances. Live delivery tracking requires an interactive map showing order status with delivery partner location updates, including an order tracking page, six order stages, partner information, and mobile interface with explicit location permission and real-time backend updates, stopping when delivery is complete and featuring a demo mode. An admin dashboard must provide order management capabilities, including order viewing, status updates, partner assignment, and menu item availability toggling, alongside a driver interface for accepting deliveries.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"ArtifactMetadata":"{\"RequestFeedback\":false,\"Summary\":\"Comprehensive guide for Brew & Bloom Café v2: Online Food Ordering & Delivery Platform. Details the high-contrast design palette, expanded menu, reactive cart, checkout workflow, Leaflet map distance & GPS routing, 6-stage order tracking, Admin Operations Dashboard, Driver Partner GPS Dispatch app, Supabase database setup, and Vercel deployment instructions.\",\"UserFacing\":true}","CodeContent":"\"# ☕ Brew & Bloom Café — Online Food Ordering & Delivery Platform (v2.0)\\n\\n## 📍 Project Location\\n```\\nC:\\\\Users\\\\Lenovo\\\\.gemini\\\\antigravity\\\\scratch\\\\brew-and-bloom\\\\\\n```\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 🎨 Design System & High-Contrast Palette\\n\\n| Token | Hex | Role |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| Deep Forest Green | `#073B32` | Primary brand tone, navbar on scroll, bestsellers bg, admin badges |\\n| Dark Espresso | `#172421` | Base dark background (Hero, Gallery, Footer), high contrast text |\\n| Vibrant Orange | `#FF7629` | Primary CTA buttons, Add-to-Cart, active route lines, highlights |\\n| Golden Yellow | `#FFC247` | Secondary CTA, Bestseller tags, stage progress accents |\\n| Warm Cream | `#FFF8EC` | Base menu section surface, drawer background |\\n| Fresh Mint | `#D9F3E5` | Veg indicators, distance badges, fresh tags |\\n| White | `#FFFFFF` | Card backgrounds, inputs, modal containers |\\n| Coral Pink & Lavender | `#FF6B6B` / `#E5DBFF` | Promo banners and special tags |\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 🗂️ Application Structure\\n\\n| Path | Purpose |\\n|---|---|\\n| [`index.html`](file:///C:/Users/Lenovo/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/brew-and-bloom/index.html) | Storefront: Hero, Promo Banners, Dynamic Menu, Bestsellers, About, Gallery, Location Map, Cart Drawer & Checkout Modal |\\n| [`order-tracking.html`](file:///C:/Users/Lenovo/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/brew-and-bloom/order-tracking.html) | Customer Live Order Tracking: 6-stage timeline, interactive Leaflet map, remaining distance, ETA, Driver card, Demo ride simulator |\\n| [`admin.html`](file:///C:/Users/Lenovo/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/brew-and-bloom/admin.html) | Kitchen & Owner Dashboard: PIN authenticated (`brew2026`), live order cards, status updater, driver assignment, menu stock toggles, sales stats |\\n| [`driver.html`](file:///C:/Users/Lenovo/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/brew-and-bloom/driver.html) | Driver Fleet App: PIN authenticated (`driver2026`), active delivery task, Google Maps navigation, genuine device GPS broadcast (`watchPosition`) |\\n| [`js/config.js`](file:///C:/Users/L\n<truncated 3424 bytes>","Description":"\"Comprehensive documentation artifact covering the upgraded food ordering and delivery platform architecture.\"","Overwrite":"true","TargetFile":"\"C:\\\\Users\\\\Lenovo\\\\.gemini\\\\antigravity\\\\brain\\\\b76faff2-d711-4aab-931a-94ff7ee7f3a8\\\\brew-and-bloom-guide.md\"","toolAction":"\"Updating deployment guide\"","toolSummary":"\"Comprehensive v2 platform guide\""}}],"truncated_fields":["tool_calls"]}
